    {
      "data": {
        "caption": {
          "content": "There were several important steps that turned the Yale Alumni Association into the Yale Club we know and love today. To learn more about the early years of the Club, click on one of the cards' buttons below to explore the 'Before the Club' story.",
          "position": "top"
        },
        "timeline": {
          "events": [
            {
              "button": {
                "collection_id": 1,
                "label": "View Story",
                "moment": 1,
                "story_id": "Q000"
              },
              "date": {
                "day": 1,
                "label": "1890",
                "month": 1,
                "year": 1890
              },
              "title": "Discussions of a clubhouse",
              "description": "Finally, in the late 1890s, several members expressed the desire to have our own clubhouse, similar to the clubhouse founded by Harvard in 1865."
            },
            {
              "button": {
                "collection_id": 1,
                "label": "View Story",
                "moment": 1,
                "story_id": "Q000"
              },
              "date": {
                "day": 15,
                "label": "1897",
                "month": 4,
                "year": 1897
              },
              "description": "On April 15, 1897, the club leaders passed around a memorandum proposing such a clubhouse, and within a month 500 signatures had been collected.",
              "title": "Collecting Signatures"
            },
            {
              "date": {
                "day": 26,
                "label": "1897",
                "month": 5,
                "year": 1897
              },
              "title": "The Yale Club incorporates"
            },
            {
              "button": {
                "label": "Explore Map",
                "newTab": true,
                "url": "https://maps.app.goo.gl/JRcFmPDNXaJmd3JL8"
              },
              "date": {
                "day": 2,
                "label": "1897",
                "month": 6,
                "year": 1897
              },
              "description": "Members decide they would rent 17 East 26th St, also known as 17 Madison Square North, from the McCoon Estate for $6,000 for three years. ",
              "image": {
                "alt": "17 Madison with annotation",
                "url": "https://stories-api-test.s3.amazonaws.com/temp/They+Lived+at+the+Yale+Club/17+Madison+N/17+Madison+in+blue.jpg"
              },
              "title": "Finding a clubhouse"
            },
            {
              "button": {
                "collection_id": 1,
                "label": "View Story",
                "moment": 2,
                "story_id": "Q000"
              },
              "date": {
                "day": 5,
                "label": "1897",
                "month": 6,
                "year": 1897
              },
              "description": "One of the first resolutions that club members made was to obtain a “Raines Law License” which would allow them to provide alcohol in the new clubhouse.",
              "image": {
                "alt": "Newspaper clipping",
                "position": "top",
                "url": "https://img.newspapers.com/img/img?user=7657948&id=542167102&clippingId=83590940&width=787&height=3993&crop=1599_924_787_3993&rotation=0"
              },
              "title": "First order of business"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
